{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28471 - PROTEIN:6154",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol may interact with Prelamin-A/C through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging through its targeting of 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is a target of both (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol and 5-Oxobrucine, which in turn targets Prelamin-A/C. While the exact mechanism by which these compounds interact with the proteasome subunit and ultimately affect Prelamin-A/C remains unclear, the shared targeting of this subunit provides a plausible link. Additionally, the indirect pathway through Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by a different compound, suggests that the relationship may involve a broader network of interactions. The evidence supports a potential role for (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol in modulating Prelamin-A/C through proteasome-related mechanisms, though further investigation is needed to clarify the precise molecular interactions involved.",
